{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=dict(action='research',rationale='Retain the executed fresh-instance endpoint and the source-owned reconstruction/termination boundary without broadening the paused configuration question.',sources=[dict(id='S_node_stop_dispatch',file='node.go',start_line=435,end_line=461,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S_log_construction',file='log.go',start_line=66,end_line=101,kind='code_observation')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['bdd27761fdf74acaa83870729e1c5433','71b0b0216b9f493dabbfcc7ac791b691','228dac2c1026445282000ac0b43f2237','S_restart_node_contract','S_restart','S_storage_contract','S_node_stop_dispatch','S_log_construction'],answered='Exploration bdd27761fdf74acaa83870729e1c5433 completed with old live learner set {4}, saved snapshot learner set empty, and fresh-instance learner set empty. Saved and reconstructed term/vote/commit were 2/1/7; caller Applied 7 yielded fresh applied 7 and follower role. All old queues were checked empty before construction, and no old response was reused. This locates the retained discrepancy in live configuration state for the tested policy; the saved snapshot and reconstruction did not retain learner 4. Source inspection separately shows newLog initializes committed/applying/applied from the compacted prefix and empty unstable state before newRaft loads HardState and caller Applied. Node stop dispatch closes that instance done channel and returns; it does not itself manage external worker queues.',remaining=['The configuration Candidate remains paused on ownership of ApplyConfChange ordering versus network snapshot restore. Reconstruction does not resolve or excuse the earlier conditional discrepancy.','No crash, partial persistence or old-completion delivery into a replacement instance was executed. Fresh channels and empty-queue construction do not establish a general worker-retirement contract.','The accepted shared read-support Fact still contains an old execution-progress note about joint history; its historical requirement basis and actual completed check/review should be distinguished if the map is next substantively revised.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Preserve the exact three exploration locators as reusable construction knowledge: after-restore delta, before-restore control and fresh reconstruction. No further repetition of these policies is needed. A next discriminator requires an explicit application/network ordering contract or an independently authorized restart-worker history; absent that, select an unread authority or replication branch from the existing overview rather than inventing a snapshot preservation duty.',question_updates={'6c76c9c951f54e83ad88674c2691aed6':{'unknowns':['The captured contracts do not explicitly assign the ordering responsibility for already-issued configuration calls versus network snapshot restore; an applicable required endpoint invariant is likewise not established.'],'resume_conditions':['Acquire a specific applicable caller contract or repository policy that settles older ApplyConfChange permission after restore, or a distinct required endpoint invariant covering that history.']}}))\njson.dump(p,open('submission-reconstruction-handoff.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_19-39-39-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-reconstruction-handoff.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
